\description{
\code{aci_filter()}, \code{aci_smoother()} and \code{aci_online()} reconstruct hidden
states: from the record up to each time, from the whole record, and from
the record up to a fixed number of steps ahead of each time. \code{lag_table()}
stores the finite-lag divergences used by the CIR estimators. The \verb{lt_*}
helpers access a table without depending on its storage representation.
\code{aci_conditional()} describes the conditional question, and
\code{aci_conditional_reduce()} carries out the model reduction its
\code{method = "reduce"} asks for. The historical \code{lt_tail_bound()} name is
retained for compatibility, but its value is a
heuristic tail estimate, not a certified mathematical error bound. A lag
table uses the complete online smoother of andreou2026cir Theorem 3
(Appendix G.1) as its reference. That
reference costs O(N) time-point work; table construction then costs work
proportional to the retained lag cells, with O(N^2) cells for a full table
in the worst case. \code{aci_online()} costs O(N) whatever the lag.
}
\section{Scheme}{

Two discretizations of the same continuous-time smoothing problem are in
use, and \code{meta$scheme} on a path says which one produced it.
\code{"backward_ode_euler"} is \code{\link[=aci_smoother]{aci_smoother()}}: the continuous backward smoothing
equations integrated with an Euler step. \code{"theorem3_discrete"} is
\code{\link[=aci_online]{aci_online()}} and the lag table's reference smoother: the exact conditional
law of the hidden state given the observed increments on the sampling grid,
under the explicit single-step discretization. They agree only to first
order in the step, so \code{\link[=aci_online]{aci_online()}} at \code{lag = Inf} does not reproduce
\code{\link[=aci_smoother]{aci_smoother()}}, and the gap grows with the length of the record rather than
settling to a constant. See the Scheme section of \code{\link[=aci_online]{aci_online()}} for the
measured size on the packaged ENSO partition. \code{aci()} reports the scheme its
own result was built under in \code{meta$smoother_scheme}.
}

